P0 OBJECTIVE (NO MORE DEBUGGING LOOPS):
exportunity.net must show Exportunity branding (name/logo/text/colors) and must NOT display any "Bourse de l'Or / gold exchange" branding.
boursedelor.com must remain unchanged.

RULES:
- Do NOT touch Bourse UX/branding.
- Implement tenant branding by domain/host header (multi-tenant) at the core level.
- After changes, redeploy and verify with a simple pass/fail checklist + screenshots.

STEP 0 -- READ FIRST (NO REDUNDANT WORK):
1) Pull latest code / review current tenant logic (where hostname -> tenantKey).
2) Identify where "Bourse de l'Or" strings, logo, title, meta, manifest, and theme colors are set.
3) Confirm Nginx Proxy Manager forwards Host headers correctly to the app container.

STEP 1 -- HARD ENFORCE TENANT RESOLUTION (THE FIX):
Implement a single source of truth function like:
resolveTenant({ host, xForwardedHost }) -> tenantKey
- If host ends with "boursedelor.com" or "www.boursedelor.com" => tenantKey = "bdo"
- If host ends with "exportunity.net" or "www.exportunity.net" => tenantKey = "exportunity"
- Otherwise default to "bdo" (or safe fallback)

Important:
- Use X-Forwarded-Host first when behind proxy, then Host.
- Log tenantKey on server start and per request (only in server logs, not UI).

STEP 2 -- APPLY BRANDING OVERRIDES FOR exportunity.net (P0 BRANDING SET):
When tenantKey="exportunity", override ALL of the following:
- App name in header: "Exportunity"
- Browser title: "Exportunity"
- Logo/mark (if shared component, swap asset by tenant)
- Any text "Bourse de l'Or" anywhere (header, footer, help pages, chatbot greeting, etc.)
- Meta tags: og:title, og:site_name, description
- PWA: manifest fields (name, short_name), icons if applicable, theme_color/background_color
- Service worker caches must not serve old branding across domains

Do NOT remove gold products/features. Only remove "Bourse de l'Or" branding on exportunity.net.
If the platform is still gold-focused internally, that's fine -- branding must be Exportunity.

STEP 3 -- CACHE / PWA SAFETY (STOP STALE BRANDING):
- Set manifest.webmanifest response headers: Cache-Control: no-store (or very low max-age) + must-revalidate.
- In SW, ensure cache keys are tenant-aware OR do not precache manifest at all.
- Bump SW cache version to force refresh.
- Ensure exportunity.net and boursedelor.com do not share cached branding artifacts.

STEP 4 -- NPM PROXY CONFIG (FORCE CORRECT HOST HEADERS):
In Nginx Proxy Manager for exportunity.net proxy host, add/ensure these headers:
proxy_set_header Host $host;
proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $host;
proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;

Then reload NPM.

STEP 5 -- DEPLOY (DO IT, DON'T ASK):
- Rebuild docker image and restart app container (src-bdo-app-1 or relevant stack).
- Confirm new version is live.

STEP 6 -- VERIFY (NO MORE DISCUSSION, PROVIDE RESULTS):
Provide this final checklist:

A) Desktop browser:
- Visit https://exportunity.net -> header shows "Exportunity", no "Bourse de l'Or" visible anywhere.
- Visit https://boursedelor.com -> unchanged.

B) API verification:
Create or reuse /api/whoami (or equivalent) to return:
{ host, xForwardedHost, tenantKey, appName }
Run and paste:
curl -s https://boursedelor.com/api/whoami
curl -s https://exportunity.net/api/whoami

C) PWA/manifest:
curl -s https://exportunity.net/manifest.webmanifest | head
must show Exportunity name/short_name.

D) Screenshots:
Attach 2 screenshots (one per domain) showing header branding.

DONE CRITERIA:
If ANY "Bourse de l'Or" branding appears on exportunity.net, the task is not done.
